  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\,{x}^{1/2}\\,{y}^{1/2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{R}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})\\text{\u00a0}(\\sqrt{y}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{y}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
